{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5914500b-3ae9-4fe4-9371-f1b01cc92ff0",
    "name": "FMS API (v1)",
    "description": "Finance Management System — `/api/v1` collection.\n\n**Synced with Postman cloud**\n- Collection UID: `31395184-5914500b-3ae9-4fe4-9371-f1b01cc92ff0`\n- Workspace: My Workspace (`813764e7-b440-4bf7-8a36-74be9c4026ab`)\n- Repo file (git source of truth): `docs/postman/FMS-API.postman_collection.json`\n- Sync metadata: `docs/postman/SYNC.md`\n\nWhen APIs change: update this JSON **and** the cloud collection (Postman MCP `putCollection` if connected). Add a collection comment describing the change.\n\n## Import (offline)\n1. Postman → **Import** → choose this file.\n2. Start the API: `cd server && npm run dev` (default `http://localhost:4000`).\n3. Collection variable `baseUrl` defaults to `http://localhost:4000/api/v1`.\n\n## Auth\nLogin/register set an **httpOnly cookie** `fms_token`. Postman’s cookie jar sends it on later requests to the same host — no Bearer header needed.\n\n**Suggested order**\n1. Health → Health check\n2. Auth → Login (Super Admin) — uses `SUPER_ADMIN_*` from `server/.env.local`\n3. Tenants → List / Create / Create admin / Update status\n4. Auth → Me / Logout\n\nAfter **Create tenant**, `tenantId` is saved automatically for follow-up requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000/api/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "tenantId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "superAdminEmail",
      "value": "superadmin@fms.local"
